      "message": "Lead the home and the review page with numbers\n\nHome and a repository's Review page now open with four tiles: what\nneeds you, who is at work, what landed today, and what waits in the\nqueue; on Review the third and fourth are disputed claims and who is\nat work here. Under them, \"Needs you\" is a panel of rows, each with a\nchip naming its lead signal, the title, where it lives, the reasons in\nplain words, the owner's avatar and its age. Home follows with your\nopen changes, what happened across your repositories as sentences that\nname who did what to which change, and the lessons attempts left\nbehind. Review follows with the landing queue and recent landings on\nthe branch, and the lessons for this repository; its rail shows who is\nat work here with the paths they hold, warning when two overlap, and\nthe last few events with their actors drawn.\n\nNobody is named by id on either page: the routes look every actor up\nonce and the views draw them. The brief's sentence is gone; its numbers\nbecame the tiles, and the link to the log stays under them.\n\nChange-Id: Ihome0129\nTask: t-6tc03xtxt9t3bv39nnkyjzgq0n\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
